cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AI Adoption Field Guide
message: >-
  If you use or adapt this guide, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Tait
    given-names: Samuel
abstract: >-
  A practical, open guide to assigning proportionate human control to
  AI-assisted workflows. It sets out a four-tier model organised on Australia's
  Guidance for AI Adoption practice 6, "Maintain human control", with practices
  1 and 2 as entry gates, a decision-rights question bank, eight oversight
  patterns, thirteen stop-rule categories including a first-class "no
  comparable case" state, adoption and benefits-realisation measures, three
  fictional worked examples, and one illustration drawn from a real documented
  incident. Mapped to the NIST AI Risk Management Framework. Not legal advice
  or certification.
keywords:
  - ai-governance
  - ai-adoption
  - risk-management
  - decision-rights
  - human-in-the-loop
  - ai-policy
  - australia
  - nist-ai-rmf
  - enterprise-ai
  - responsible-ai
